          "site_admin": false
        },
        "body": "A release tag currently triggers automatic publication, so the existing path cannot honor the operator's publication hold. This change separates read-only exact-main preparation from manual publication through the protected `rcc-production` environment. It retires automatic tag creation and the historical recovery publisher, verifies the actual nine assets and source-bound full11/native/JAT/compiler evidence, and rejects existing tags/releases and malformed index URLs.\n\nRefs #118. **PUBLICATION HOLD remains: no tag, release, publication dispatch, or implicit operator GO.** This draft proposes the workflow correction; it does not establish hosted release qualification.\n\nValidation at head `83ddea8a8e8304692b53ffe38d9c6bd03ee1d370`: 37 focused unittest checks passed independently, all 12 workflow YAML files parse, Python compilation and diff checks pass. Independent review rejected seven malformed index variants and confirmed the two prior review findings are fixed. Root also ran all 37 focused tests successfully. Historical native receipts were used to test receipt parsing only; no receipts are rebound to this new source.\n\nRemaining gates: exact-head hosted/native/full11 acceptance; configured/readable protected approval policy and credentials; actual preparation-run nine-asset independent verification, source/version/index/checksum/archive/architecture/compiler/signing/install/trust/offline/rollback evidence; security finding disposition (15 dashboard alerts unidentified through current API403); separate explicit operator GO. Performance #125 is independent and not a technical release gate.\n\nDocumentation: `docs/release-process.md` and workflow README describe preparation, approval, retired legacy paths and signing/token limits.\n\n### CI correction and current head\n\nCurrent head: `bb2759e3fe9b2121e1ce8134a028d7d27d4d1936`, tree `75f1a13f81b932c4017973dcaa0642ba05758985`. This is a fast-forward through preserved `83ddea8` and `ed8f8fb` checkpoints; no source history was rewritten.\n\nThe first labelled candidate run https://github.com/joshyorko/rcc/actions/runs/38140726296 failed on two stale workflow-contract tests (gate exit10, tee0). Its raw ZIP/log/exit receipt are preserved and root independently verified. The correction tests the manual publisher's Homebrew preflight-before-tag and release-before-dispatch ordering and isolates the native YAML job. Additional negative checks reject compiler suffixes and boolean/float exit receipts.\n\n**Root independently ran all 131 Python script unit tests from clean current head: exit0.** The existing mocked gate-sequence unit test needs a temporary ignored `build/rcc` hash fixture; it was never executed as RCC and was removed. This is source/unit acceptance only, not a real full11 or native qualification. Independent review of production corrections and root review of the final test-only delta are complete. New exact-head hosted/native/full11 checks are required; prior-source checks are not rebound. Publication remains held; no tag or release was created.",
        "created_at": "2026-10-11T12:48:11Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-11T14:37:27Z",
